  "id": "frozen-noise",
  "term": "frozen noise",
  "definition": "Frozen noise is a single noise segment that is reused identically in a repeating pattern. When the same segment is played back continuously without pauses, it creates repeating frozen noise, a stimulus used to study how people hear periodicity, faint events, and pitch-like qualities in noise.",
